cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the article in preferred-citation."
title: "KGEval: transparency and reusability assessment of biomedical knowledge graphs"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Code and data accompanying an assessment of 17 biomedical knowledge graphs
  (KGs) against 28 transparency and reusability subcriteria covering access,
  provenance, documentation, versioning, evaluation and licensing. Includes the
  evaluation table, a rule-based mapping (validated against the schema) of each
  KG's node and edge labels to
  Biolink Model v4.4.5, and code to reproduce the manuscript figures.
